It's a bug;
**The behavior is correct by accident when the clustered index is enabled;**
When the clustered index feature is enable/disable during our development, the bug disappears or regression;
Without a test case to cover it, we did not recognize it.

The bug is caused by the mess operation of `stmtctx.AddAffectedRows`, sometimes we do it in [tables.AddRecord](https://github.com/pingcap/tidb/blob/master/table/tables/tables.go#L798) and sometimes we do it in [executor.updateRecord](https://github.com/pingcap/tidb/blob/5d8b99feef47bcae3eb51fff95c30ceabb55e2f5/executor/write.go#L232), when calling update, it might be repeat twice.

I believe handle `stmtctx.AddAffectedRows` in executor is better, because `UpdateRecord` may involve `RemoveRecord  + AddRecord` when the primary key change, in the table package's AddRecord it's lack of that context to know the following on RemoveRecord.
